From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:12:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GBM: detect immutable DRM properties

IsPropertyImmutable() asks drm_property_type_is() for
DRM_MODE_PROP_IMMUTABLE, but that helper compares the type bits of a
property, and immutability is a flag outside of them, so every property
is reported mutable. On vc4 the zpos of the primary plane is an
immutable range of 0 to 0, and MoveOnTopOf() then tries to set it,
which the kernel rejects with EINVAL. Test the flag itself.

Fixes: 2e5eccbc2595 ("CDRMObject: Add IsPropertyImmutable for drm props")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMObject.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMObject.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMObject.cpp
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@ std::optional<bool> CDRMObject::IsProper
   if (property == m_propsInfo.end())
     return {};
 
-  return static_cast<bool>(drm_property_type_is(property->get(), DRM_MODE_PROP_IMMUTABLE));
+  return (property->get()->flags & DRM_MODE_PROP_IMMUTABLE) != 0;
 }
 
 bool CDRMObject::SupportsProperty(std::string_view name)
